"""Shared presentation guidance for user-facing agent answers."""

USER_FACING_RESPONSE_FORMAT_GUIDANCE = """Format the user-facing answer as plain text with optional lightweight Markdown; never emit HTML. Use a blank line between distinct paragraphs. For a multi-step explanation, timeline, or several records, give a brief introduction and put each item on its own bullet or numbered-list line instead of combining everything into one paragraph. Keep a greeting or simple answer short; when a greeting is followed by an offer or question, put them on separate lines. Use a natural line break whenever it improves readability. Use **bold** sparingly for an important result, protocol, or status, and *italics* sparingly for a relevant technical term. Emojis are optional: use them only when they make a list or status easier to scan, and do not decorate every sentence. When including a URL, format it as a Markdown link with a short descriptive label; only link to URLs explicitly present in approved evidence, and never invent or alter a URL. Preserve supplied identifiers, numbers, dates, time zones, evidence, and uncertainty exactly; do not add unsupported facts or omit a material caveat. Choose the layout that best fits the user's question and language."""
